# Line endings are pinned to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, the founder's global core.autocrlf=true checks these files out as
# CRLF while storing them as LF. That is invisible on one machine and churns whole
# files into every diff the moment a second machine, a CI runner, or a container
# touches the repo. Pinning it here makes the repo self-describing: the setting
# travels with the code instead of living in one person's global git config.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect and leave binary files alone, so this stays
# correct if an image ever lands in docs/.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the file types actually in the repo, so intent survives a future
# edit to the blanket rule above.
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
